      "math_academy_id": "e-3980",
      "problem": "The equation $\\log_{16}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{b} = 4.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare $\\log_{16}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ with $\\log_{b}{a} = x,$ we get $a = 4,$ $b = 16,$ and $x = \\dfrac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to $16^{1/2} = 4,$ which is also equivalent to $\\sqrt{16} = 4.$ Consequently, $b = 16.$",
